Original commit body from a1e924a62f36ec79a7963fca694f00e82edd5f31:

database-query-linker declared ELEVEN host languages in its second CNF
conjunct while _find_source_files scans four globs (**/*.py, **/*.js, **/*.ts,
**/*.java) and dispatches to three scanners. Eight of the eleven named neither
a pass whose output it reads nor a file it opens -- and it consumes no host
analyzer's output at all: it takes ctx.repo_root and re-reads the query side
from disk.

TOO WIDE IS THE FALSE-ALL-CLEAR DIRECTION HERE, and falsification cannot see
it. A clause is an inner-OR, so any single member satisfies it, and eight
never-scanned languages kept the clause satisfiable on repositories where this
linker could not possibly have read anything. find_falsified_dependencies is
backward-looking and catches only a clause that is too NARROW, so this was
invisible to the detector by construction -- found by reading the body.

Repaired to [["sql"]], the shape WI-dinum shipped for graphql-linker: name the
pass that supplies the edge DESTINATION, not where the source pattern was
found. sql's kind="table" symbols are the only pass output this linker
consumes. depends_on is declarative -- read by validate_pass_dependencies and
the falsification report, never by execution -- so no activation changes.

The new test derives its justification rather than asserting it: it AST-walks
the linker module for its own glob constants, so the claim "this linker reads
files itself" is evidence in the test, not prose in a comment.

RESIDUAL, enumerated rather than assumed and deliberately NOT swept:
subprocess-linker declares 9 languages and scans only **/*.py; orm-linker
declares 8 and scans only **/*.py; http-linker declares 13 and scans 9;
message-queue-linker declares 9 and reads no ctx.symbols at all. But most
siblings DO read ctx.symbols, so unlike this one they may carry a real host
dependency and each needs its own verification -- a mechanical sweep here would
be the same mistake this row is about. Recording the scan capability on
activation is also left open: LinkerActivation has no file-shape field, so that
is a core-dataclass change with its own axis-declaration obligations.

